{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe air in Paris is thick with dust and ambition. I spent the afternoon at the Louvre, walking the long halls with Raumer and Panofka. It is the last day before the gallery opens to the living painters, a strange inversion of value, but the old masters still hold the ground. The light in the afternoon was poor, but the shadows in the corners gave the canvases a certain depth that the midday sun strips away.\n\nWe dined at a small table near the Seine; the wine was acceptable, the service tedious. I paid four francs for a meal that offered little more than sustenance, though the view of the river was a fair compensation. I have read your last letter; Immanuel’s progress with his Latin is noted, though I fear his attention to detail is still lacking. A boy who does not master the small rules has no business claiming the large freedoms.\n\nI am tired. I shall take my snuff and rest.\n\nYour affectionate\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219429,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":215,"prompt_tokens":1127,"total_tokens":1342,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Zn0YZjZg6XJ87jltZIkEisPpU7Tmy8um","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1127,"prompt_ms":1178.125,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0453637976929901,"prompt_per_second":956.604774535809,"predicted_n":215,"predicted_ms":5140.036,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.018859813084113,"predicted_per_second":41.63394964548886}}